      "blurb": "Start, middle, end: same letter, different outfits.",
      "canDo": "You can spot these letters at the start, middle and end of a word",
      "teach": [
        {
          "title": "Letters hold hands",
          "info": "Most letters join to the next letter on their left, so they have up to four shapes: on their own, at the start, in the middle and at the end of a word. The core shape (and the dots!) always stays the same.",
          "glyph": "ب  بـ  ـبـ  ـب"
        },
        {
          "title": "Shape families",
          "info": "This unit's letters: ص  ض  ط  ظ  ع  غ  ف  ق. Same family, same body: look at the dots and small marks to tell them apart.",
